WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.220
In the Game of Thrones books, lots of characters
have secret identities.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:08.540
Like, Sansa pretends to be Alayne, Varys pretends
to be Rugen.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.670
Maynard Plumm is actually Bloodraven, who’s
also the three-eyed crow.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:16.180
Robert Strong is the Mountain, Griff is Jon
Con.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.310
Young Griff is Aegon Targaryen, who might
actually be a Blackfyre.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.699
The list goes on and on, and one of the coolest
of these secret identities is Alleras.

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:31.690
Alleras is a student at the Citadel in Oldtown,
which is like the Westerosi university.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:37.320
He’s involved with Sam Tarly, Marwyn the
Mage, and Jaqen H’ghar, who seek secrets

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.710
in the Citadel.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:43.000
Alleras is a minor character, but he’s got
a secret of his own.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.320
Cause he is actually a she – she’s Sarella
Sand, a bastard daughter of Oberyn Martell.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.460
The most obvious evidence that Alleras is
Sarella is that the name “Alleras” is

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:56.460
“Sarella” backwards.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.640
But also, we know that Sarella’s father
is Oberyn Martell, of Dorne, and Sarella’s

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:06.950
mother is “a trader” “from the Summer
Isles” . Alleras is the same – his mother

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:11.990
is “a trader” from the Summer Isles, and
his father is “a Dornishman” . Alleras

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:17.000
even looks like Oberyn – they both have
black eyes and black hair with a “widow’s

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.140
peak” . At one point, Alleras says “I
am no lord’s son” – which is true, cause

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.659
she’s actually a lord’s daughter.

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:29.450
Alleras is “always smiling, as if he [knows]
some secret jape” . And the evidence shows

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:34.310
that his “secret” is that she is actually
Sarella Sand.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.250
So who is Sarella?

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:41.461
In the show, Oberyn Martell has three daughters,
but in the books, he has eight, called the

00:01:41.461 --> 00:01:47.461
Sand Snakes . Sarella is the fourth-born,
now nineteen years old . In Book 4, the three

00:01:47.461 --> 00:01:52.710
eldest Sand Snakes, Obara Nymeria and Tyene,
wanna start a war with the Lannisters , to

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.840
avenge the deaths of Oberyn and aunt Elia.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.910
To prevent this war, their uncle Doran arrests
the Snakes – Obara, Nym, Tyene, and the

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:04.770
young ones are captured , but Doran doesn’t
arrest Sarella.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.640
Because Sarella’s not in Dorne – she’s
in Oldtown as Alleras.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.670
Doran says “Unless she returns to Dorne,
there’s naught I can do about Sarella”.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:19.379
“Leave her to her … game” . So it doesn’t
sound like Sarella is working with Doran or

00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:21.180
with the other Sand Snakes.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.599
What is her “game”?

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:25.760
What’s she doing in Oldtown?

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.409
Sarella loves learning.

00:02:27.409 --> 00:02:31.379
On a visit to some ruins, Sarella “turned
over rocks, brushed sand off … mosaics,

00:02:31.379 --> 00:02:35.980
and wanted to know everything there was to
know about the people who had lived” there

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:41.010
. So maybe Sarella came to the Citadel university
because she wants to learn stuff.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:45.629
Her father Oberyn did the same thing . But
the Citadel doesn’t accept women – which

00:02:45.629 --> 00:02:49.849
must be why Sarella disguises herself as a
guy – Alleras.

00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:53.669
And Alleras does well at the Citadel, earning
“three links of his maester’s chain”

00:02:53.669 --> 00:02:59.129
in one year, meaning she masters three subjects
really fast . And she seems to care about

00:02:59.129 --> 00:03:03.919
the values of the Citadel, telling Lazy Leo
that he “shame[s] the Citadel by being one

00:03:03.919 --> 00:03:09.669
of” them . Also, Nymeria mentions that Sarella
loves the city of Oldtown . So Sarella is

00:03:09.669 --> 00:03:15.540
smart, she wants to learn, she loves the Citadel
and Oldtown and that’s probably why she’s

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.540
there.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:22.559
But Sarella slash Alleras slash Sarelleras
gets involved in much more than just study.

00:03:22.559 --> 00:03:25.840
At the start of Book 4, Alleras practices
archery.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.879
He uses a goldenheart bow, which connects
to his Summer Islander heritage . He talks

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:35.969
with his student friends about the rumours
of the dragon queen Daenerys in the east . And

00:03:35.969 --> 00:03:40.430
this guy Leo reveals there’s a “glass
candle burning” in the chambers of Marwyn

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.430
the Mage.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:46.029
A glass candle is a candle of obsidian, and
for centuries, these candles have been impossible

00:03:46.029 --> 00:03:47.029
to light.

00:03:47.029 --> 00:03:52.700
But now, they burn again , which shows that
magic and dragons have returned to the world.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.420
“Old powers waken” Leo says.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:04:00.430
“Shadows stir” . And Alleras is really
interested in this talk of magic and dragons

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:06.370
. So by the end of the book, he becomes an
ally of the guy with the candle – Marwyn.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.629
Marwyn is a rebel professor.

00:04:08.629 --> 00:04:13.489
He travels to strange distant places, studies
with strange people like Qyburn and Mirri

00:04:13.489 --> 00:04:19.199
Maz Duur , and he writes books about prophecy
. He’s an expert on magic, but most maesters

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:24.060
don’t trust magic , so they discredit Marwyn
. Marwyn claims there’s a conspiracy by

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:29.009
the maesters to suppress magic and dragons
– watch this video for more.

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:34.600
So Marwyn’s a little crazy, maybe, but he
totally knows things about magic and prophecy

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.590
– partly because he has this glass candle.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:43.900
Cause glass candles let you see across distances
and enter dreams – Marwyn uses his to watch

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:44.900
and learn.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:49.780
He sees Sam arrive at the Citadel, so Marwyn
gets Alleras to bring Sam to him.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:54.889
And Sam tells them about his experiences at
the Wall with white walkers, and Melisandre,

00:04:54.889 --> 00:05:01.310
and how Maester Aemon thinks Daenerys is Azor
Ahai – the hero prophesied to save the world.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:05.169
So Marwyn leaves and heads east to meet Daenerys
.

00:05:05.169 --> 00:05:10.660
This leaves Sam at the Citadel with Alleras,
and with a guy called Pate – who is actually

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.280
the Faceless assassin Jaqen H’ghar in disguise.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:19.759
Jaqen is there possibly to steal a book called
The Death of Dragons – go watch the Jaqen

00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:20.759
video.

00:05:20.759 --> 00:05:27.919
But also, Sam has an old horn, which is probably
the Horn of Winter which can destroy the Wall.

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:32.729
Also also, there’re ironborn raiding around
Oldtown , and Euron Greyjoy’s making an

00:05:32.729 --> 00:05:39.660
eldritch mass blood sacrifice nearby . So
there’s a lot of intense magic shit converging

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.660
on Oldtown.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:43.090
And Alleras seems connected.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:48.840
Alleras’ friends call him the Sphinx, because
a sphinx has the face of a human, body of

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:53.580
a lion, and wings of a hawk – it’s made
up of different parts, just like Alleras is

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:58.950
both Dornish and Summer Islander . But the
sphinx might also refer to Alleras’ secret

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.099
identity.

00:06:00.099 --> 00:06:05.139
There are statues of sphinxes at the Citadel
– one male and one female, which might hint

00:06:05.139 --> 00:06:08.800
at Sareleras’ male and female identities.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.139
But the sphinx symbol goes even deeper.

00:06:11.139 --> 00:06:16.110
Cause on the way to Oldtown, Maester Aemon
tells Sam that “the sphinx [is] the riddle,

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:21.030
not the riddler” . Sam wonders if Alleras
the Sphinx might be the sphinx Aemon meant

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:26.750
. Maybe the idea is that Alleras is not a
“riddler” who’ll tell you a riddle , Alleras

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:31.050
is “the riddle”, as in in his secret identity
as Sarella is “the riddle”.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:36.159
But why would Aemon talk about the secret
identity of some minor character he’s never

00:06:36.159 --> 00:06:37.159
met?

00:06:37.159 --> 00:06:41.690
Aemon mentions the sphinx alongside talk of
dreams, glass candles, eggs, and the three

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:46.400
heads of the dragon – which seems to be
the idea that three dragonriders will ride

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:51.550
Dany’s three dragons . Alleras also mentions
the three heads of the dragon , and he is

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.500
involved with glass candles.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.740
So maybe Alleras is connected to this Targaryen
dragon stuff.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:02.870
In Book 5, Tyrion finds a Valyrian sphinx
– “A dragon queen” with the head of

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.110
a woman and body of a dragon.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:10.639
She seems to be “missing” “Her king”,
a male half-human half-dragon . If the female

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:14.800
dragon-sphinx is Daenerys, the male could
be Jon Snow.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:19.460
He’s part dragon cause’s he’s half Targaryen,
and he’s probably the rightful “king”

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:23.941
of Westeros , and he could be Dany’s future
husband, and he could be one of the three

00:07:23.941 --> 00:07:25.949
heads who rides a dragon.

00:07:25.949 --> 00:07:31.669
Jon might be the sphinx Aemon meant, and this
could link back to Alleras if Alleras and

00:07:31.669 --> 00:07:37.499
Sam uncover Jon’s true parentage at the
Citadel, like Sam and Gilly do in the show.

00:07:37.499 --> 00:07:43.840
So the riddle of the sphinx is still confusing,
but it seems to connect Jon and Dany and the

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:47.000
Targaryen dragons with Sarelleras.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.300
What does all this mean for her future?

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:54.279
It looks like Alleras will be Sam’s study
buddy at the Citadel . They might learn important

00:07:54.279 --> 00:07:58.999
secrets about white walkers or Azor Ahai or
Jon’s parentage.

00:07:58.999 --> 00:08:03.639
But with Jaqen H’ghar around, they might
also get caught up in his plot to steal that

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:05.110
dragon book.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:10.419
Marwyn and Alleras seem to wanna support Daenerys
– but Alleras could also become Dany’s

00:08:10.419 --> 00:08:11.419
enemy.

00:08:11.419 --> 00:08:17.129
Cause in Book 5, Dany rejects a marriage alliance
with Dorne , and one of Dany’s dragons kills

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:23.689
Sarella’s cousin Quentyn . So maybe Sarelleras
will use her archery skills to slay a dragon.

00:08:23.689 --> 00:08:26.740
Jaqen’s book, the Death of Dragons, might
help.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:32.339
At the same time, Euron brings sorcery and
destruction on the city Sarella loves – will

00:08:32.339 --> 00:08:34.680
she fight to protect Oldtown?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:39.430
So, like a Sphinx, Sarellaras is made of different
parts.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:45.170
She’s a Sand Snake, daughter of Oberyn Martell
of Dorne, but she’s also a Summer Islander,

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.890
with a goldenheart bow.

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:52.279
She’s a student of the Citadel, with a love
for Oldtown and ties to Marwyn, and she also

00:08:52.279 --> 00:08:55.940
seems connected to the Targaryens, Jon and
Dany.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:09:01.161
This complex combination of conflicting loves
and loyalties define the Sphinx as one of

00:09:01.161 --> 00:09:04.709
the most interesting minor characters in the
series.

